cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AstroCausal Engine"
abstract: >-
  A real-time 2D simulator in which gravitational interaction propagates at the
  finite speed c, implemented through per-body multi-resolution history ring
  buffers. It integrates retarded Newtonian gravity, the Paczynski-Wiita
  pseudo-potential, 2.5PN radiation reaction in the Damour-Deruelle form, and a
  Velocity Verlet integrator, and renders gravitational field heatmaps whose
  value at every pixel is read back at that pixel's own retarded time. It is an
  educational and visualization tool, not numerical relativity: it does not
  solve the Einstein field equations.
authors:
